{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Jacob lived.</b> Rashi explains: why is this parashah closed off? etc. And one may ask: but Yosef continued to reign after Jacob's passing! One may answer that as soon as Jacob passed away they began to enslave them little by little. And further, Rashi explained that he sought to reveal the end [of the exile] and it was sealed from him. And if you ask: from where did he know the end? One may answer: from the rungs of the ladder that he dreamed, for he saw the prince of Esav ascending the rungs, as Rashi explained in the parashat ויצא." "<b>And Jacob lived in the land of Egypt.</b> Why does the verse mention the tally of his life in the land of Egypt? Because we find that Yosef was with his father before his sale seventeen years, and just as Jacob sustained Yosef seventeen years, so Yosef sustained and provided for him seventeen years in return. Of this it is said: ״אלה תולדות יעקב יוסף בן שבע עשרה שנה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:15.056439201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}